==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*stōdą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*sta-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*stə-||stand, set}}.  Cognate with Old High German {{term|stuot||herd of horses|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Stute||mare|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|stóð|lang=non}} (Swedish {{term|sto||mare|lang=sv}}). The Indo-European root is also the source of Albanian {{term|shtazë||animal, beast|lang=sq}} and Old Slavic ''stado''<!--wrong script for Old Slavic-->

